    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c7e1ac32_33767188",
        "filename": "third_party/CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T22:06:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m confused as to why this is needed? The `add_subdirectory` on 195 should define `Vulkan::Headers`. Are the VVL and loader not checking for the cmake target before they check for the package?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "fd4aee5a8b158b0e0e72e5bf02ef4bb69bdc383e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d26f1552_42d35e4a",
        "filename": "third_party/CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T22:14:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When add_subdirectory runs for those targets they use find_packages to find Vulkan::Headers since they are expecting it to already be installed. So they will only find the system version at configure time.",
      "parentUuid": "c7e1ac32_33767188",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "fd4aee5a8b158b0e0e72e5bf02ef4bb69bdc383e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f37f39eb_0a114e35",
        "filename": "third_party/CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T22:16:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But this is adding the vulkan headers, so they _should_ be available. I thought FindPackage checks if the target exists already? In the past I\u0027ve built things this way and it was fine, VVL and loader would use the headers that I added. Is this a recent change where they broke cmake upstream so this doesn\u0027t work anymore?",
      "parentUuid": "d26f1552_42d35e4a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "fd4aee5a8b158b0e0e72e5bf02ef4bb69bdc383e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ff798b77_39f1bb2b",
        "filename": "third_party/CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000250
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-10T22:24:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "find_packages from what I can tell doesn\u0027t use targets in CMake build, it is install cmake packages.\n\nWe have had warnings for a long time about the versions being wrong, which indicated the system version was being used. There is a change that landed for the Loader atleast that now expects an useable version to be found at runtime, functionally turning that warning into a build failure.",
      "parentUuid": "f37f39eb_0a114e35",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "fd4aee5a8b158b0e0e72e5bf02ef4bb69bdc383e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "79079c0a_d3fa2538",
        "filename": "third_party/CMakeLists.txt",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 224,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000257
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-02-11T01:51:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Doing add_subdirectory is how Amber and VKB both worked, they\u0027d add everything and it worked. It\u0027s possible they changed things recently which broke stuff, but in that case I think we should fix it upstream.\n\nDo you have a bot this fails on where I can se what\u0027s happening? Or some way to check what cmake is doing?",
      "parentUuid": "ff798b77_39f1bb2b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 197,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 224,
        "endChar": 53
      },
      "revId": "fd4aee5a8b158b0e0e72e5bf02ef4bb69bdc383e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
